{"name":"Valley View","hex":"#b0c376","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Valley View","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Madison County, Kentucky.\nAn unincorporated community in Benton County, Missouri.\nAn unincorporated community in Jackson Township, Ste. Genevieve County, Missouri.\nA village in Cuyahoga County, Ohio .\nAn unincorporated community and census-designated place in Hegins Township, Schuylkill County, Pennsylvania. \nA census-designated place in Spring Garden Township, York County, Pennsylvania.\nA minor city in Cooke County, Texas.","An unincorporated community in Madison County, Kentucky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Valley_View"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valley View, Ooty","blocks":[{"text":"Valley View is a tourist spot in Ooty, India. It is located on the Ooty Coonoor road at a distance of 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) from Ooty bus stand and constitutes ward number 5 of the Nilgiris Lok Sabha constituency. It has views over the Ketti valley, and is an important tourist centre in Ooty. Ketti valley is sometimes referred to as the Switzerland of Southern India. The valley extends from the Deccan Plateau to the Coimbatore plains and is one of the largest valleys in the world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_View%2C_Ooty","wikidata":"Q7912255"},{"title":"Valley View, South Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Valley View is a suburb of Adelaide, South Australia. It spans three separate local government areas. They are the City of Salisbury, the City of Port Adelaide Enfield, and the City of Tea Tree Gully. The suburb's boundaries are defined by the intersection of Walkleys, Grand Junction and North East Roads in the south, and Wright and Kelly Roads in the north and east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Valley_view_golf_course.jpg/330px-Valley_view_golf_course.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_View%2C_South_Australia","wikidata":"Q7912257"},{"title":"Valley View (Romney, West Virginia)","blocks":[{"text":"Valley View is a mid-19th-century Greek Revival residence and farm overlooking the South Branch Potomac River northwest of Romney, West Virginia, United States. The house is atop a promontory where Depot Valley joins the South Branch Potomac River valley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Valley_View_Romney_WV_2013_01.jpg/330px-Valley_View_Romney_WV_2013_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_View_(Romney%2C_West_Virginia)","wikidata":"Q16902507"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Rose_bud_%286027707280%29.jpg/500px-Rose_bud_%286027707280%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Rose_bud_%286027707280%29.jpg/1280px-Rose_bud_%286027707280%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Rose_bud_%286027707280%29.jpg/50